cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, data, or analysis, please cite the associated manuscript."
title: "Opioid exposure is largely transcriptionally quiescent in spinal cord microglia: a multi-omics dissection of the neuropathic-pain activation hub universe and its RUNX1-anchored, repurposable-analgesia target space"
abstract: "Reproducible computational re-analysis of public mouse spinal-cord microglia transcriptomics (GSE117320) and LINCS L1000 (GSE92742) showing that long-term morphine exposure is transcriptionally quiescent in microglia, whereas neuropathic pain drives a 3,069-gene activation program converged on six hub genes anchored to RUNX1 and the NF-kappaB axis, with honest negative/modest validation layers and phenazone nominated as a brain-penetrant repurposing lead."
